# DTF tier manifest: osv-positional-findings
#   (artifact-keeper#4079, #4081, #4150, #4080; all shipped in 1.11.0)
# Profile-set: filesystem + upstreams.mock-osv (api.osv.dev resolves to a
# stdlib-python OSV mock trusted through CUSTOM_CA_CERT_PATH; the oracle
# registers every advisory and can flip the feed into an outage).
#
# The dependency scanner had no end-to-end coverage at all: `osv` and
# `querybatch` were unreferenced in this repo, and the pinned-CVE gates depend
# on live OSV.dev. Here a generic repository holds pip manifests
# (<dir>/requirements.txt, parsed by the dependency scanner on every image)
# naming run-unique PyPI packages the mock alone knows about, and the oracle
# reads the `dependency` scan row and its findings straight from Postgres.
#
# THE BUGS (all RED on 1.10.0)
#   #4081  Every finding's affected_component was deps.first(): a manifest
#          listing a clean package before a vulnerable one filed the finding
#          against the clean one (and the SBOM join named the wrong component).
#   #4150  querybatch answers ids only; the scanner never fetched the record,
#          so findings had no cve_id, no fixed_version and the title
#          "Vulnerability <id>"; a batch-wide dedup reported one CVE shared by
#          two packages only once. Fixed: /v1/vulns/{id} hydration (budget
#          OSV_RECORD_FETCH_BUDGET_SECS), per-dependency dedup.
#   #4079  The batch response was flattened and cached under EVERY dependency
#          of the batch for the 1 h advisory TTL, so a later artifact naming
#          only the clean package inherited the vulnerable one's finding.
#   #4080  A feed outage (transport error, non-2xx, unparseable body) returned
#          an empty list and the scan was graded `complete`: a false all-clear.
#          Fixed: graded `partial`.
#
# THE GATES
#   (CONTROL) every image: a manifest with no advisories is queried and grades
#     complete with 0 findings; after the outage ends the same package is
#     asked again and reported; the backend reached the mock as api.osv.dev.
#   (FIX) #4081, #4150 x2, #4079, #4080: RED on 1.10.0, GREEN on 1.11.0 and
#     later.
#
# NOT GATED: the GitHub Advisory half of #4080 (a 403 from api.github.com
# degrades, no token does not): it needs GITHUB_TOKEN and a second TLS
# hostname; OSV_RECORD_FETCH_BUDGET_SECS exhaustion (a slow /v1/vulns keeps
# the bare finding, not degraded).
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: ~20 API calls plus scan polling.
PROFILES="storage.filesystem upstreams.mock-osv"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
